    id: 'input.joystick', tag: 'STATIC',
    statement: 'Read in full in WW.EXE and in the control menu of SETUP.EXE (obj1+0x8c50 to +0x8e8d): the joystick path of the input. Configuration words, as file offsets of WACKY.CFG (the first piece is read to obj2+0x1ee1c, the third to obj2+0x17128, cfg.read): for player 1 the six words 0x1c, 0x1e, 0x20, 0x22, 0x24 and 0x26 are the stick centre x and y and the left, right, up and down thresholds and the word 0x2e is the "use the joystick" flag (SETUP stores 1 when the Joystick or Game Pad choice is picked, 0 for Keyboard; obj2+0x21736); for player 2 the six words 0x4b2 to 0x4bc are the same six values and the word 0x4ae is a "use the keyboard" flag (SETUP stores 1 for Keyboard, 0 otherwise); the words 0x4aa (player 1) and 0x4ac (player 2) are set to 1 by SETUP\'s "Game Pad/4 button stick" choice (SETUP obj2+0x8100, +0x8102, +0x8104). The routine at obj1+0x4b00 (the player number in ax; called before a race, obj1+0x5c05) copies one player\'s six values to obj2+0x28b5c, +0x28b5e, +0x28b52, +0x28b3c, +0x28b3e and +0x28b48 and the port masks to obj2+0x28be4, +0x28be6, +0x28be8 (player 1: 1, 2 and 3, the first stick of the game port; player 2: 4, 8 and 0xc, the second), and sets the word obj2+0x28c8a to 1, which switches the stick off, when the player\'s flag chooses the keyboard (obj1+0x4b00 to +0x4c09). The routine at obj1+0x2784b clears the four direction bytes obj2+0x28cd5 (left), +0x28cdd (right), +0x28cd6 (up) and +0x28cd3 (down), and unless the word obj2+0x28c8a is 1 writes 0 to the game port 0x201, reads the port in a loop that adds the masked values into the word totals obj2+0x28b54 (x) and +0x28b56 (y; halved afterwards) until the stick bits drop or the counter overflows (which sets the word obj2+0x28c74 to 1, no stick found), then compares twice x with the x centre (and twice y with the y centre, likewise): when 2x is below the centre by at least the left threshold it sets the left byte, when above it by at least the right threshold the right byte, and the same for y with the up and down thresholds (obj1+0x2784b to +0x279e6). The left and right bytes feed input.steer-flags, so the stick steers like the first two keys. With the option "Use Joystick DOWN as BRAKE and UP as HAND BRAKE TURN" (the word 0x862 for player 1 and 0x864 for player 2, SETUP obj2+0x84b8 and +0x84ba, set when the "Use option" choice is picked, SETUP obj1+0x2fc3 to +0x2ff7) the game raises the brake button (obj2+0x28b44) when the down byte is set and the hand brake turn button (obj2+0x28b46) when the up byte is set, for player 1 only when the stick is on (obj1+0x1f51a to +0x1f55d), for player 2 through the words obj2+0x28cc6 and +0x28cc7 in two-player races (obj1+0x220c4 to +0x2111a). All three installed WACKY.CFG files hold 0 for every one of these words except the player 2 keyboard flag 0x4ae, which is 1: both players use the keyboard. Not observed at run time; how SETUP.EXE fills the thresholds from three stick positions is setup.joystick-calibration.',
